    INTENTS.push({ tag: "comp_networking", patterns: ["what does dns do on the internet","dns on the internet","what is ip address","how does wifi work","router and modem","what is dns","bandwidth and speed","what is a server","network types lan wan","ping kya hai","5g network","internet cables under the ocean"],
        responses: ["📡 **Networking — how devices actually talk:**\n- **IP address** = your device's home address on a network (like 192.168.1.5 at home; every website has one too). **DNS** = the phonebook translating names → numbers (google.com → 142.250.x.x)\n- **Modem** brings internet INTO your home (from the cable/fibre/air) · **Router** shares it to all your devices & runs WiFi 📶\n- **WiFi** = radio waves at 2.4/5 GHz — short-range, through walls, shared air (that's why it slows when everyone streams!)\n- **LAN** = small local network (home/school) · **WAN** = wide network — the internet itself\n- **Bandwidth** = pipe width (Mbps) · **Latency/ping** = travel time (ms) — gamers care about PING most! ⚡\n- The internet literally runs on **undersea fibre cables** (~500+ of them!) carrying 99% of international data — sharks once bit them 😂\n- **5G** = newer generation mobile network: more capacity, lower latency. Packets of your message bounce router→ISP→server→back in milliseconds!"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "comp_coding", patterns: ["which language runs in the browser","browser programming language javascript","what is coding","programming languages","how to learn coding","what is python","what is javascript","compiler and interpreter","what is an algorithm","coding kaise sikhe","first programming language for beginners","what is a bug in coding","binary code"],
        responses: ["💻 **Coding = teaching computers with precise instructions:**\n- A computer understands only **binary** — billions of 1s and 0s (switches ON/OFF). Programming languages are the friendly bridge: you write `print(\"Hello\")`, a **compiler/interpreter** translates it to machine code\n- **Algorithm** = the recipe (step-by-step logic) · **Code** = the recipe written in a language · **Bug** 🐛 = a mistake (the term came from an actual moth stuck in a 1947 computer!)\n- **Popular languages:** Python 🐍 (beginner-friendly, AI & data), JavaScript (runs EVERY website — and BitBot's own brain! 😉), Java & C++ (apps, games, engines), HTML/CSS (not 'programming' but the web's skeleton & skin), SQL (talks to databases)\n- **How to start:** pick ONE language (Python or JS), learn loops-conditions-functions, then BUILD tiny projects (calculator, quiz game, personal site). Typing tutorials ≠ learning — building = learning 🔨\n- Fun truth: this whole website — games, chat, and me — is just HTML+CSS+JS. Code is a superpower anyone can learn!"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "comp_security", patterns: ["what is hacking","malware and virus","cyber security","what is a computer virus","how do hackers steal passwords","phishing","two factor authentication","what is encryption","data breach","hacker se kaise bache","white hat hacker"],
        responses: ["🛡️ **Cyber security — defending your digital life:**\n- **Malware** = evil software: **virus** (attaches to files), **worm** (spreads itself), **trojan** (gift-wrapped trap), **ransomware** (locks your files for money 💰), spyware\n- **Hacking** = breaking into systems. **White hats** 🤠 = ethical hackers companies PAY to find weaknesses; **black hats** = criminals\n- **Phishing** = fake messages/sites tricking you into giving passwords ('YOUR ACCOUNT IS BLOCKED, click here!' — NEVER click 😤)\n- **Encryption** = scrambling data so only the right key can read it (WhatsApp's 🔒, https://, your saved passwords)\n- **2FA** = password + a second proof (OTP/app code) — turns a stolen password into a useless one\n\n**Your armour:** long unique passwords (a password MANAGER helps), 2FA everywhere, update your apps (updates patch holes!), never share OTPs — NOT even with 'bank officials' 🚫, be suspicious of free-gift links. The safest password is the one you never type into the wrong place!"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "comp_mobile", patterns: ["difference between ram and storage","ram vs storage in a phone","how do smartphones work","android vs iphone","what is an app","mobile processor","what is ios","touch screen technology","phone camera megapixels","app store play store","mobile ke parts","what is a sim card","oled vs lcd screen"],
        responses: ["📱 **Smartphones — a supercomputer in your pocket:**\n- **Brains:** the **SoC** (system-on-chip) — CPU (thinking) + GPU (graphics/games) + NPU (AI) on one silicon square. Android flagships: Snapdragon, MediaTek Dimensity · Apple: A-series/M-series. Android = Google's open OS (Samsung, Xiaomi, Vivo...) · iOS = Apple's closed OS (iPhones only)\n- **Screen:** OLED (each pixel glows itself → true blacks 🔋) vs LCD (one backlight). Touch = a grid sensing the tiny electrical change from your finger (so gloves don't work!)\n- **Camera:** megapixels ≠ quality; sensor size + software (AI processing) matter more 📸\n- **Memory:** RAM (multitasking desk) vs storage (cupboard — photos, apps)\n- **Apps** = programs from Play Store/App Store; a **SIM** = your network ID card; **IMEI** = the phone's fingerprint\n- Your phone is 1000× more powerful than the computers that guided Apollo 11 to the Moon 🚀 — and mostly used for reels. No judgement. 😄"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "comp_future", patterns: ["what does vr stand for","vr in gaming","future technology","what is virtual reality","augmented reality","quantum computer","robots and automation","metaverse","3d printing","self driving cars","future me kya hoga","technology trends"],
        responses: ["🔮 **Tomorrow's tech, today's headlines:**\n- **VR (Virtual Reality)** — headset transports you INTO a digital world 🥽 · **AR (Augmented Reality)** — digital stuff layered on the real world (Pokémon GO, furniture-preview apps, smart glasses)\n- **Quantum computers** — use qubits (0 AND 1 at once!) to crush problems normal computers can't: new medicines, unbreakable codes. India has its own Quantum Mission 🇮🇳\n- **Robots & automation** — factory arms → humanoids → surgical robots (da Vinci) → drones delivering blood in Rwanda & medicines in India 🩸\n- **Self-driving cars** — cameras + radar + AI chauffeurs (Tesla/Waymo); level 5 (steering wheel optional) is still the boss fight\n- **3D printing** — printing houses, rocket engines, even body parts layer by layer 🖨️\n- **Metaverse** — shared 3D internet where you 'go' places as an avatar\n- **Brain-computer interfaces** (Neuralink) — controlling devices with thoughts, already helping paralyzed patients\n- The pattern: every wild tech becomes boring in ~15 years. The kids building skills NOW will pilot all this. That's you! ⚡"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "comp_database", patterns: ["what is sql used for","sql query language","what is a database","sql meaning","how is data stored","dbms","what is a table in database","google stores data where","data warehouse","what is cloud storage","database kya hai","what is big data"],
        responses: ["🗄️ **Databases — organized memory for machines:**\n- A **database** = data stored so it's easy to find, update & protect. Think a super-powered, queryable spreadsheet\n- **Table** = rows (records) × columns (fields). Your chat profile might be one row: username, score, email\n- **DBMS** = the manager software; **SQL** (Structured Query Language) = how you ask it things: `SELECT * FROM users WHERE score > 100` — 'show me everyone who beat 100!' 😄\n- Types: **relational** (MySQL, PostgreSQL — neat tables) vs **NoSQL** (MongoDB — flexible docs, great for apps)\n- **Cloud storage** = databases & files living on giant server farms (Google Drive, AWS, Azure — some data centers are the size of towns!)\n- **Big Data** = oceans of information (every search, swipe, purchase) that AI trains on — 5 V's: volume, velocity, variety, veracity, value\n- Every like, every highscore, every message online lives in some database right now — including, probably, yours 📊"] });

    /* ══════════ SPORTS batch ══════════ */
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "sports_football", patterns: ["football rules","who won the fifa world cup in 2022","world cup winner argentina 2022","football game","how many players in football","fifa world cup","offside rule","messi ronaldo","football positions","premier league","isht ball world cup winner","football ke niyam","who is the football king"],
        responses: ["⚽ **Football — the world's #1 sport (4 billion fans!):**\n- **11 vs 11**, two 45-min halves; score in the net = goal; no hands (except the goalkeeper in the box!)\n- **Positions:** goalkeeper 🧤, defenders, midfielders (the engine room), forwards/strikers\n- **Offside** = attacking player can't lurk behind the last defender when the ball is passed to them (the rule everyone argues about 😤)\n- **FIFA World Cup** (every 4 years) = the biggest event on Earth: **Argentina won 2022** (Messi's crowning, vs France on penalties 🇦🇷) · 2026 will be hosted by USA-Canada-Mexico with 48 teams!\n- **The GOAT debate:** Lionel Messi 🐐 (8 Ballon d'Ors, 2022 WC) vs Cristiano Ronaldo 💪 (900+ career goals, plays at 40!). Pick your side wisely.\n- Leagues: English Premier League, La Liga (Spain), Champions League\n- India loves it too: ISL, and the 2017 U-17 World Cup was hosted here 🇮🇳"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "sports_hockey", patterns: ["wizard of hockey","dhyan chand the wizard","national game of india","hockey game","field hockey","is hockey the national game of india","hockey world cup","dhyan chand","indian hockey history","hockey players positions","hockey ke bare me","hockey stick and ball","sultan azlan shah"],
        responses: ["🏑 **Hockey — India's golden legacy:**\n- **Fun fact first:** India has NO officially declared national game! But hockey FEELS like one because of the history 👇\n- **Golden era:** India won Olympic hockey GOLD **8 times** (1928–1980), including 6 in a row! 🥇\n- **Major Dhyan Chand** — 'The Wizard': so magical that at the 1936 Berlin final, legend says Hitler offered him German citizenship; his birthday (29 August) = National Sports Day 🇮🇳\n- Modern game: fast artificial turf, drag-flicks, video umpire. 11 vs 11, four 15-minute quarters\n- **India today:** men's team won Bronze at Tokyo 2020 (first medal in 41 years!) and repeated at Paris 2024 🥉; the women's team (2021 semis) inspired a nation\n- Big events: Hockey World Cup (Bhubaneswar-Rourkela host!), Pro League, Champions Trophy\n- Other hockey: ice hockey 🧊 (NHL, Canada's passion) & roller hockey. Field hockey rules the Olympics!"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "sports_olympics", patterns: ["olympics","what do the olympic rings represent","five rings of the olympics","olympic games","olympic rings meaning","where are next olympics","olympic medals","paralympics","commonwealth games","asian games","olympics kitne saal me","first olympics history","india at olympics","neeraj chopra gold"],
        responses: ["🏅 **The Olympics — humanity's biggest sports party:**\n- **Ancient origins:** started in Olympia, GREECE ~776 BCE (they even paused wars for the Games!); revived in 1896 by Pierre de Coubertin — Athens hosted the first modern Olympics\n- **5 rings** (blue, yellow, black, green, red on white) = the inhabited continents united; at least one of these colours is in EVERY national flag 🌍\n- Held every **4 years**; Summer & Winter alternate every 2 years\n- **Motto:** Citius, Altius, Fortius – Communiter = Faster, Higher, Stronger – Together\n- **India's moments:** Neeraj Chopra's javelin **GOLD at Tokyo 2020** (first track & field gold for India! 🥇 + silver at Paris 2024), 8 hockey golds, PV Sindhu & Sakshi Malik's medals, Manu Bhaker's Paris 2024 double bronze\n- **Paralympics** — elite athletes with disabilities, held right after (often India out-medals its Olympics count! 💪)\n- Also: Commonwealth Games (Britain's ex-family), Asian Games, Youth Olympics. Next Summer Olympics: **Los Angeles 2028**! 🏟️"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "sports_badminton", patterns: ["badminton game","shuttlecock","pv sindhu","saina nehwal","badminton court","how is badminton scored","thomas cup uber cup","indian badminton players","badminton ke niyam","fastest racket sport"],
        responses: ["🏸 **Badminton — the fastest racket sport on Earth:**\n- The shuttlecock can smash at **490+ km/h** (faster than F1 cars!) — that's a world record smash 💥\n- **Singles** (1v1) or **doubles** (2v2); games to **21 points**, best of 3; every rally scores (rally point system)\n- Played over a net (1.55 m) on a court split by service boxes — needs speed, wrist-snap & chess-like tactics\n- **Shuttlecock** = cork + 16 goose feathers (or nylon for practice) — the only asymmetric ball... not-ball in sports!\n- **India's pride:** 🇮🇳\n  · **PV Sindhu** — Olympic silver (2016) + bronze (2020), World Champion 2019\n  · **Saina Nehwal** — Olympic bronze (2012), world #1 in 2015\n  · **Prakash Padukone** — All England champion 1980 (the pioneer!)\n  · **Satwik-Chirag** — men's doubles world #1 pair, Thomas Cup winners 2022 🏆\n- Tournaments: All England, Indonesia Open, BWF World Tour, Olympics. Grab a racket — it's India's most medal-friendly sport!"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "sports_chess", patterns: ["where was chess born","chess originated in which country","chess game","how to play chess","checkmate","chess pieces and moves","viswanathan anand","magnus carlsen","chess opening","gukesh chess","shatranj kaise khelein","chess origin india","grandmaster title"],
        responses: ["♟️ **Chess — the royal mind-sport (born in INDIA!):**\n- Ancestor: **Chaturanga**, invented in India ~6th century (the four army divisions → modern pieces); went to Persia ('shah mat' = 'the king is dead' → **checkmate**!), then Europe\n- **64 squares**, 16 pieces each: King (1 step, protect at all costs!), Queen (most powerful — any direction ♛), Rooks (straight lines 🏰), Bishops (diagonals), Knights (L-shape — the ONLY piece that jumps! 🐴), Pawns (1 step forward, capture diagonally, dream of promotion)\n- Special moves: castling (king safety), en passant, pawn promotion (reach the end = new queen!)\n- **Goal:** checkmate — the king is attacked and CANNOT escape. Stalemate = draw!\n- **Legends:** 🇮🇳 Viswanathan Anand (5× World Champion, the 'Tiger of Madras'), **Gukesh D** — became the YOUNGEST World Champion ever (18, in 2024!) 🔥, Magnus Carlsen (Norway)\n- Titles: Grandmaster (GM) is the top — India now has 80+ GMs, a superpower surge 📈\n- Chess improves memory & planning — and it's FREE to start. Checkmate your boredom!"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "sports_athletics", patterns: ["athletics events","running events in olympics","marathon distance","100m sprint","javelin throw","long jump high jump","track and field","neeraj chopra javelin","relay race","athletics ke khel","usain bolt record"],
        responses: ["🏃 **Athletics (track & field) — the purest sports:**\n\n**Track (running):**\n- Sprints: 100m (the glamour event!), 200m, 400m · Middle: 800m, 1500m · Long: 5000m, 10,000m\n- **Marathon = 42.195 km** (named after the Greek battle of Marathon — a soldier reportedly ran that far to deliver victory news!)\n- Hurdles (jump barriers while sprinting), **Relays** (4×100m — baton passing = pure teamwork 🤝)\n\n**Field (jump & throw):**\n- Long jump, high jump, triple jump, pole vault\n- Shot put, discus, hammer, **javelin** 🥇\n\n**Records & heroes:**\n- **Usain Bolt** — 100m in **9.58s** (~44 km/h top speed!), double-triple Olympic champion ⚡\n- **Neeraj Chopra** — javelin GOLD Tokyo 2020 (87.58m throw), silver Paris 2024; India's track-and-field king 👑\n- Hima Das (sprint), Avinash Sable (steeplechase), KM Deeksha... India's athletics is rising!"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "sports_esports", patterns: ["esports","competitive gaming","is gaming a sport","esports tournaments","pro gamers","esports india","bgmi valorant tournaments","gaming careers","esports olympics","professional gaming kya hai"],
        responses: ["🎮 **Esports — when gaming goes pro:**\n- **Esports** = organized competitive video gaming: tournaments, teams, coaches, prize pools (The Dota 2 'International' once offered $40 MILLION! 💰)\n- Popular titles: Valorant, CS2, League of Legends, Dota 2, BGMI/Free Fire (mobile esports is HUGE in India 🇮🇳), Rocket League, even chess & racing sims\n- Pro players train 8+ hours daily: aim, strategy, VOD-review, teamwork, fitness (yes — reflexes need a healthy body!) 🧠💪\n- **India's scene:** BGMI/Valorant tournaments, ESL India, national esports awards; medal events at Asian Games 2023 (esports debuted!) 🥇\n- Streaming created the other half: Twitch/YouTube gamers earn by entertaining while playing\n- **Is it a 'real sport'?** Debate rages — but the Olympics are literally planning the 'Olympic Esports Games' (first edition 2025, Saudi Arabia) 🏟️\n- And hey — you're on an ARCADE site right now. The highscore board is where every esports legend begins 😎"] });

    /* ══════════ HEALTH batch ══════════ */
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "health_diet", patterns: ["balanced diet","junk food effects","why is breakfast important","healthy eating habits","what to eat for energy","fast food vs healthy food","obesity causes","diet for students","junk food kyu nuksan karta hai","how much water to drink daily"],
        responses: ["🥦 **Eating smart (no boring lectures, promise):**\n- **Balanced plate:** ½ veggies/fruits 🥗 · ¼ protein (dal, eggs, paneer, chicken) · ¼ carbs (roti, rice) + a bit of healthy fat\n- **Breakfast = brain fuel:** skip it and by 11am your focus crashes; eggs/paratha-curd/oats-fruits beat skipping\n- **Junk food trap:** chips & cola = calorie bombs with near-zero nutrients (sugar spikes → crash → crave more — it's DESIGNED to be addictive 😤). Once in a while = fine; daily = weight gain, tiredness, weak immunity\n- **Water:** ~8–10 glasses/day (more in summer/sports). Thirst is already mild dehydration! 💧\n- **Student hacks:** carry fruit instead of chips · namkeen+chai study snack → roasted chana 🥜 · sugary drink → nimbu paani/lassi · late-night Maggi → keep some eggs/bread\n- **Obesity** = consistent calorie surplus + low activity. The fix is boring but works: real food, moving daily, sleeping 8h 😴"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "health_fitness", patterns: ["benefits of exercise","how much exercise do i need","workout for beginners","warm up and cool down","why is physical activity important","exercise for students","gym at what age","cardio vs strength","roz vyayam karna chahiye","fitness tips for teens"],
        responses: ["💪 **Exercise — the closest thing to a cheat code:**\n- **Recommended:** 60 min/day of activity for teens (WHO!), incl. bone-strengthening stuff 3× a week\n- **What it does:** stronger heart & bones 🦴, better sleep, LESS stress & anxiety (endorphins = natural happy chemicals), sharper memory & focus (yes, exercise literally grows brain cells!), confidence boost\n- **Types:** **Cardio** (running, cycling, swimming, dance, cricket! — trains heart & stamina) vs **Strength** (push-ups, squats, gym — builds muscle; teens can lift with proper form & supervision)\n- **Warm-up** (5 min light movement) = oil for your joints, prevents injuries · **Cool-down** (stretching) = helps recovery\n- **No gym? No problem:** surya namaskar, jumping jacks, skipping 🪢, stairs instead of lift, football/cycling with friends, even active gaming breaks\n- **Consistency > intensity:** 20 min daily beats 3 hours once a month. Your body keeps score — start today, thank yourself at 30! 🏃"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "health_hygiene", patterns: ["personal hygiene","why wash hands","brushing teeth","how germs spread","bathing and cleanliness","hygiene habits for students","wash hands with soap","saaf safai ka mahatva","how to keep surroundings clean","nail and hair hygiene"],
        responses: ["🧼 **Hygiene — the invisible shield:**\n- **Handwashing with soap** (20 seconds — sing Happy Birthday twice 🎂) kills the #1 disease courier: your hands! Before eating, after toilet, after playing outside\n- **Germs travel:** air (cough/sneeze droplets — elbow-cover!), contaminated water & food, touch surfaces → touch face → entry! 🦠\n- **Daily armour:** bath daily · brush 2× (morning + BEFORE BED — night plaque parties are real 🪥) · clean nails (germ hotels!) · fresh clothes, esp. socks & uniforms · tie/cover long hair while eating-cooking\n- **Home hygiene:** clean drinking water (boil/filter), covered food, garbage out daily, no standing water (mosquito = dengue & malaria's taxi 🦟), toilets kept clean\n- **Why it matters:** historically, soap + clean water saved MORE lives than any medicine. Diarrhoea & infections still hit hardest where hygiene slips\n- Bonus: a clean room = a calmer brain. Desk tidy, marks... slightly tidier too 😄"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "health_diseases", patterns: ["do antibiotics work on viruses","antibiotics against viruses or bacteria","common diseases","how do diseases spread","fever cold cough","dengue malaria","what is vaccination","bacterial vs viral","communicable and non communicable diseases","tb cholera typhoid","bimari se kaise bache","why do we get fever"],
        responses: ["🤒 **Diseases — know your enemy:**\n\n**Communicable** (spreads person→person or via vectors):\n- **Viral:** common cold, flu, chickenpox, dengue (mosquito 🦟), polio — antibiotics DON'T work on viruses!\n- **Bacterial:** TB (lungs, long cough), typhoid (dirty water/food), cholera (severe diarrhoea), tetanus (dirty wounds)\n- **Protozoan:** malaria (female Anopheles mosquito) — India fights it hard\n- Spread routes: air droplets, contaminated water/food, insects, touch, blood\n\n**Non-communicable** (don't spread): diabetes, heart disease, asthma, cancer — mostly lifestyle + genes\n\n**Fever** = your body turning UP the heat to cook germs — it's a battle sign, not the enemy itself 🌡️\n\n**Vaccination** = training your immune system with a 'wanted poster' of the germ, so real attacks fail. It's why smallpox is EXTINCT and polio is nearly gone. Get your shots, wash hands, drink clean water, sleep well — the 4-piece armour! 🛡️"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "health_firstaid", patterns: ["first aid","what to do for burns","first aid for cuts","emergency numbers india","cpr basics","what to do in an accident","snake bite first aid","nosebleed treatment","first aid kit items","ambulance number","emergency me kya karein"],
        responses: ["🚑 **First aid — the first 5 minutes can save a life:**\n\n**Emergency numbers (India): 112** (all-in-one!) · 108 ambulance · 100 police · 101 fire\n\n- **Burns** 🔥 — cool RUNNING water for 10–20 min. NEVER toothpaste/ice/oil! Cover loosely, pop no blisters\n- **Cuts/bleeding** — press firmly with clean cloth (pressure stops bleeding!), raise the limb, clean & bandage once slowed. Deep/rusty wound → doctor (tetanus shot!)\n- **Nosebleed** — sit up, lean FORWARD (not back!), pinch soft nose 10 min\n- **Snake bite** 🐍 — keep calm & still (movement spreads venom), remove rings, note the time, get to hospital — do NOT cut, suck, or tourniquet\n- **Fracture** — don't move the limb, support it with cardboard/wood splint, ice pack wrapped in cloth\n- **Unconscious, not breathing** — **CPR**: push hard & fast in chest center (100–120/min — the beat of 'Stayin' Alive' 😄), let someone call 112\n\n**First-aid kit:** bandages, antiseptic, gauze, tape, scissors, ORS, paracetamol, thermometer, gloves. Know it, don't show it! 💪"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "health_mind", patterns: ["exam stress","how to control tension","mental health","anxiety before exams","feeling pressured by studies","how to relax my mind","depression signs","talk to someone about problems","padhai ka tension","meditation for students","how to stay calm"],
        responses: ["🧘 **Your mind matters as much as your marks:**\n- **Stress isn't weakness** — it's the brain's alarm. A little stress = fuel; too much = fog, headaches, stomach aches, sleep loss 😣\n- **Exam-stress toolkit:**\n  1. **Plan** — a timetable kills 50% of the panic (fear feeds on vagueness)\n  2. **Break it down** — 'study science' is scary; 'finish 3 questions of ch.2' is doable ✅\n  3. **Breathe** — 4-7-8 breathing (in 4s, hold 7s, out 8s) × 4 rounds calms your body in 2 minutes\n  4. **Move** — a 15-min walk resets the brain better than an extra hour of staring\n  5. **Sleep 7–9h** — memory is SAVED during sleep. All-nighters literally delete your prep 🧠💾\n- **Talk to someone** — friends, parents, a teacher you trust. Feelings shrink when spoken\n- If sadness/hopelessness stays for 2+ weeks, or you can't function — tell an adult & see a doctor. Asking for help is BRAVE, not broken ❤️\n- **iCall helpline: 9152987821** · Tele-MANAS: **14416** (free, 24×7, Indian languages)\n- One exam never decides a life. You are more than your marks 🌱"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "health_yoga", patterns: ["yoga","yoga benefits","surya namaskar","pranayam breathing","yoga asanas for students","international yoga day","yoga kya hai","meditation vs yoga","ayurveda basics","yoga for concentration"],
        responses: ["🧘‍♂️ **Yoga — India's gift to the world (5,000+ years old!):**\n- **Yoga** = union of body, breath & mind. Patanjali's Yoga Sutras organized it ~2,000 years ago\n- **Asanas** (postures): Tadasana (height & posture), Vrikshasana 🌳 (balance), Bhujangasana (back strength), Shavasana (the deceptively hardest one — total relaxation 😴)\n- **Surya Namaskar** — 12 poses saluting the sun; a full-body workout in 5 minutes, great before school!\n- **Pranayama** (breath control): Anulom-Vilom (alternate nostrils — calm focus), Bhramari (humming bee — instant stress-buster 🐝)\n- **Benefits (science-backed):** flexibility, core strength, lower blood pressure, reduced anxiety, BETTER CONCENTRATION & memory — literally a student superpower 📚\n- **21 June = International Yoga Day** — India proposed it in 2014, 177 countries agreed in record time 🇮🇳\n- **Ayurveda** = yoga's sister science: food, herbs & routines in balance with your body type (dosha)\n- Start small: 10 min daily of surya namaskar + anulom-vilom. Free gym, ancient edition!"] });

    /* ══════════ ENGLISH batch ══════════ */
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "eng_vocabulary", patterns: ["what is a synonym","what is an antonym","synonym antonym meaning","what are synonyms","what are antonyms","synonyms and antonyms","how to improve vocabulary","word meanings","new english words daily","strong vocabulary tips","opposite words","one word substitution","english words for exams","shabd bhandar kaise badhaye","reading vocabulary"],
        responses: ["📖 **Vocabulary — your word arsenal:**\n\n**Synonym/antonym power pairs:**\n- happy ↔ miserable · brave ↔ cowardly · ancient ↔ modern · scarce ↔ abundant · humble ↔ arrogant · begin ↔ conclude\n- Synonyms for 'very good': excellent, superb, outstanding, stellar ⭐\n\n**How to actually grow it (no cramming!):**\n1. **Read daily** — stories, comics, newspapers; the #1 proven method 📚\n2. **3-word rule** — learn just 3 new words a day = ~1,000/year\n3. **USE them** — a word you don't use within a week escapes\n4. Keep a **word journal** (phone notes work)\n5. Break big words: 'bio-logy' = life-study, 'tele-vision' = far-seeing — roots (Latin/Greek) unlock thousands!\n\n**One-word substitutions (exam favourites):** one who loves books = bibliophile 🤓 · something that can't be avoided = inevitable · a speech without preparation = impromptu · one who studies stars = astronomer\n\nWords are a game character's stats — every new word = +1 charisma! 😄"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "eng_idioms", patterns: ["idioms and phrases","english idioms with meaning","break a leg meaning","piece of cake idiom","idioms for exams","what does raining cats and dogs mean","common english idioms","phrases muhavare","once in a blue moon","idiom kya hota hai"],
        responses: ["🗣️ **Idioms — English's secret codes (meaning ≠ literal words):**\n- **Break a leg** = good luck! (theatre superstition 🎭)\n- **Piece of cake** = very easy (this topic is one 😄)\n- **Raining cats and dogs** = raining heavily 🌧️\n- **Once in a blue moon** = extremely rare\n- **Hit the books** = study hard 📚 · **Burn the midnight oil** = work late into the night\n- **Spill the beans** = reveal a secret · **Let the cat out of the bag** = same family! 🐱\n- **Bite the bullet** = face something painful bravely\n- **Under the weather** = feeling sick 🤒\n- **Ball is in your court** = your turn to decide\n- **Costs an arm and a leg** = very expensive 💸\n- **Barking up the wrong tree** = accusing/pursuing the wrong thing\n- **Beat around the bush** = not coming to the point (I just did it for you 😆)\n\nHindi equivalents exist too — 'naach na jaane aangan tedha', 'ghar ki murgi dal barabar'. Every language winks at its speakers!"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "eng_proverbs", patterns: ["proverbs with meaning","famous english proverbs","all that glitters is not gold","proverbs for students","haste makes waste","old sayings and wisdom","kahawat ke bare me","moral sayings","proverbs class 7","a stitch in time"],
        responses: ["🦉 **Proverbs — compressed wisdom from a thousand years:**\n- **'All that glitters is not gold'** — shiny ≠ valuable (fake friend alert ⚠️)\n- **'A stitch in time saves nine'** — fix small problems early, before they explode\n- **'Haste makes waste'** — rushing ruins work (exam speed trap!)\n- **'Where there's a will, there's a way'** — determination finds a path 💪\n- **'Practice makes a man perfect'** — reps beat talent that doesn't work\n- **'Honesty is the best policy'** — lies need maintenance; truth runs free\n- **'Don't judge a book by its cover'** — surfaces deceive\n- **'Actions speak louder than words'** — doing > saying\n- **'Rome wasn't built in a day'** — big goals need patience\n- **'When in Rome, do as the Romans do'** — adapt to local customs\n- **'Two heads are better than one'** — teamwork 🤝\n\nHindi treasures too: 'boond boond se ghada bharta hai', 'kar bhala to ho bhala'. Proverbs are cheat codes for essays AND life — quote one, sound wise instantly 😎"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "eng_writing", patterns: ["format of a formal letter","formal letter format for exams","write an essay","essay writing help","letter writing format","how to write an essay","email writing format","application writing to principal","paragraph writing tips","formal and informal letter","essay structure introduction body conclusion","notice writing","report writing format","letter kaise likhe"],
        responses: ["✍️ **Writing skills — formats that fetch full marks:**\n\n**Formal letter/application:**\nSender's address → Date → Receiver's designation+address → Subject → 'Sir/Madam' → Body (3 short paras: intro, detail, request) → 'Yours faithfully' → Name\n\n**Informal letter:** address, date, 'Dear Rahul', friendly body, 'Yours lovingly' 😊\n\n**Essay = hamburger 🍔:**\n- **Intro** (top bun) — hook + your main idea/thesis\n- **Body paras** (fillings) — one point each: Point → Explain → Example\n- **Conclusion** (bottom bun) — restate + leave a thought. NEVER introduce new stuff here!\n\n**Email:** clear subject line, greeting, short body, sign-off. Professional = no 'hiiii', no ALL CAPS\n\n**Notice:** box it! Name of issuing body, 'NOTICE', date, heading, content (what-when-where-who), issuer name\n\n**Golden rules:** plan for 2 min before writing, vary sentence lengths, cut 'very/really', spell-check by reading ALOUD. Writing is thinking made visible 🧠→📄"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "eng_speaking", patterns: ["english speaking tips","how to speak english fluently","improve pronunciation","english conversation practice","how to speak confidently in english","english bolna kaise sikhe","fluency vs accuracy","overcome fear of speaking english","accent training"],
        responses: ["🎤 **Spoken English — fluency is a gym, not a gift:**\n1. **Speak from day one** — broken English beats silent perfect English! Everyone starts with mistakes 😤→😄\n2. **Think in English** — stop translating from Hindi in your head; label your day ('I'm brushing', 'bus is late')\n3. **Shadowing** — play a YouTube video/podcast, repeat lines right after the speaker, copying rhythm & tone 🎧\n4. **Read aloud** 10 min daily — your tongue needs training like a cricketer's wrist\n5. **Record yourself** — cringe once, improve forever 📱\n6. **Find speaking partners** — friends, family, Discord servers, or even... me! 😜\n7. **Learn PHRASES, not just words** — 'Could you please…', 'I think that…', 'On the other hand…' — ready-made bricks\n- **Pronunciation focus:** the 'th' sound, word STRESS (PHOtograph vs phoTOGraphy vs photoGRAPHic!), and the schwa /ə/ — English's laziest, most common sound\n- **Confidence secret:** listeners care about your MESSAGE, not your accent. Slow down, smile, speak 🌟"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "eng_reading", patterns: ["benefits of reading books","how to build reading habit","best books for students","reading comprehension tips","why should we read","book recommendations for beginners","reading habit kaise banaye","fiction vs nonfiction","newspaper reading benefits","kitabe padhne ke fayde"],
        responses: ["📚 **Reading — downloading other people's brains:**\n\n**Why read?**\n- Vocabulary & writing improve automatically (no effort!)\n- Focus & memory get stronger — reading is weightlifting for the brain 🏋️\n- Stress drops (6 minutes of reading cuts stress ~68% — more than music or tea!)\n- Empathy grows — living inside characters' heads teaches people-skills\n- Knowledge compounds: 20 pages/day ≈ 30 books/year 😮\n\n**Building the habit:** start TINY (10 pages/day), same time+place (bed works best), keep the book visible, quit boring books without guilt (life's too short!), track streaks\n\n**Beginner-friendly picks:** 🇮🇳 Ruskin Bond (our hills, our hearts), Sudha Murty, APJ Abdul Kalam's 'Wings of Fire' 🔥, R.K. Narayan's Malgudi days · 🌍 Harry Potter, Percy Jackson, Wonder, The Alchemist, Sherlock Holmes\n\n**Comprehension hack (exams):** read the QUESTIONS first, then hunt in the passage. Answers are always IN the text!\n\nNewspaper bonus: current affairs + editorial = free UPSC prep 😄"] });

    /* ══════════ STUDY & CAREER ══════════ */
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "study_focus", patterns: ["how to concentrate on studies","cant focus on studying","distracted while studying","phone distraction solution","pomodoro technique","how to study without getting bored","focus badhane ke tarike","best time to study","attention span tips","study environment"],
        responses: ["🎯 **Focus — the superpower of this decade:**\n\n**The Pomodoro Technique 🍅 (game-changer):**\n25 min full-focus study → 5 min break → repeat 4× → long 20-min break. The timer makes your brain treat it like a match, not a marathon!\n\n**Kill distractions:**\n- Phone in ANOTHER room (notifications off isn't enough — out of sight!) 📵\n- One tab/one book/one subject at a time — multitasking is a myth, task-switching is a tax\n- Fixed study spot = brain auto-enters 'study mode' there (desk, not bed!)\n\n**Boost focus:**\n- Study the HARDEST subject first (morning brain = boss brain 🧠)\n- Active > passive: solve, recall, teach-to-an-empty-chair, flashcards — never just re-read & highlight (feels productive, isn't)\n- Water + light snack; heavy meals = sleep mode 😴\n- 2-min rule: can't start? Commit to just 2 minutes — starting is 90% of the battle\n- Sleep & exercise = the focus foundation, no hack replaces them\n\nDistraction wins championships... said no one ever. Pomodoro on, phone off! ⏱️"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "career_guide", patterns: ["career options after 10th","which stream to choose after 10th","science commerce arts stream","career after 12th","what to become in future","career counselling","future career choices","stream selection confusion","competitive exams after 12","mere liye kaunsa career sahi hai"],
        responses: ["🧭 **Career guide — choose a path, not a panic:**\n\n**After 10th — the three classic streams:**\n- 🔬 **Science** (PCM/PCB) → engineering (JEE), medicine (NEET), research, IT, space, defence tech\n- 💰 **Commerce** → CA (Chartered Accountancy), CS, banking, finance, business, economics\n- 🎨 **Humanities/Arts** → UPSC/civil services, law (CLAT), psychology, journalism, design, history — the 'creative + power' lane\n- Plus: **Vocational/skill routes** — design, animation, coding bootcamps, hospitality, sports, content creation (yes, these are real careers now!)\n\n**How to choose (the 3-circle rule):**\n1. What am I CURIOUS about? (you'll study it for years — interest = fuel)\n2. What am I GOOD at? (skills grow fastest where talent meets effort)\n3. What does the WORLD pay for? (demand check 🔍)\nOverlap of all three = your sweet spot!\n\n**Truths:** marks open doors, SKILLS keep you in the room · careers change (AI era!) — learn to learn · no stream is 'superior', toppers exist in all three · a decision at 15 can be upgraded at 18, 21, 30. Explore, ask seniors, try things — curiosity IS career counselling 🚀"] });

