    INTENTS.push({ tag: "gk_symbols", patterns: ["national symbols of india","national animal bird flower","national anthem of india","national song of india","jan gan man","vande mataram","national emblem of india","national fruit tree river","rashtriya prateek","national heritage animal aquatic"],
        responses: ["🇮🇳 **India's national symbols — the identity kit:**\n- 🐅 **Animal:** Bengal Tiger · 🦚 **Bird:** Peacock · 🌸 **Flower:** Lotus · 🥭 **Fruit:** Mango · 🌳 **Tree:** Banyan\n- **Heritage animal:** Elephant 🐘 · **Aquatic animal:** Ganges river dolphin · **Reptile:** King cobra · **Bird of heritage:** Great hornbill\n- 🏞️ **River:** Ganga · ⛰️ **Mountain (heritage):** Himalayas · **Museum...** okay enough categories 😄\n- **Emblem:** the Lion Capital of Ashoka at Sarnath — 3 visible lions, motto **'सत्यमेव जयते'** (Satyameva Jayate = Truth alone triumphs), from the Mundaka Upanishad\n- **Flag:** tricolour — saffron (courage & sacrifice), white (peace & truth), green (growth & auspiciousness), Ashoka Chakra = 24 spokes of progress ⚙️\n- **Anthem:** 'Jana Gana Mana' — Rabindranath Tagore (52 seconds, full version) · **Song:** 'Vande Mataram' — Bankim Chandra Chatterjee\n- **Calendar:** Saka calendar · **Currency:** ₹ · **Language (official):** Hindi in Devanagari + English (22 scheduled languages total!)\n\nKnow them — quiz-night royalty! 👑"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "gk_awards", patterns: ["indian film song won the oscar","which song won the oscar","oscar award","naatu naatu oscar","indian oscar winner","bharat ratna","national awards of india","nobel prize","indian nobel laureates","oscar awards india","gallantry awards","param vir chakra","civilian awards padma","khel ratna award","award ke bare me batao"],
        responses: ["🏆 **Awards — humanity's gold stars:**\n\n**India's civilian honours (descending):**\n1. **Bharat Ratna** 💎 — highest civilian award (since 1954): recipients include C. Rajagopalachari, APJ Abdul Kalam, Lata Mangeshkar, Sachin Tendulkar (first sportsperson!), and in 2024 — MS Swaminathan, Karpoori Thakur, Advani... medal = peepal leaf shape\n2. **Padma Vibhushan** → 3. **Padma Bhushan** → 4. **Padma Shri** — given each 26 January\n\n**Gallantry (bravery):** Param Vir Chakra (wartime highest — only 21 ever!), Maha Vir Chakra, Vir Chakra · peacetime: Ashoka Chakra 🎖️\n\n**Sports:** Major Dhyan Chand Khel Ratna (highest), Arjuna Award, Dronacharya (coaches)\n\n**Nobel Prize** 🇸🇪 (since 1901, from Alfred Nobel's will — dynamite inventor's guilt-gift!): Peace, Physics, Chemistry, Medicine, Literature, Economics.\n**Indian/India-linked laureates:** Tagore (1913, Literature — first Asian!), CV Raman (1930, Physics 🌈), Mother Teresa (1979, Peace), Amartya Sen (1998, Economics), Kailash Satyarthi (2014, Peace), Venkatraman Ramakrishnan (2009, Chemistry)\nOscar: Bhanu Athaiya (costume, 1983), Satyajit Ray (honorary), 'Smile Pinki', **RRR's 'Naatu Naatu' 🕺 (2023)**!"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "gk_books", patterns: ["famous books and authors","who wrote ramayana","holy books of religions","famous indian authors","autobiography books","book ka author","who wrote wings of fire","books by gandhi nehru","bestselling books world","religious books names"],
        responses: ["📚 **Books & authors — the knowledge leaderboard:**\n\n**Ancient/epic India:** Ramayana — Valmiki · Mahabharata — Ved Vyasa · Geeta (part of Mahabharata) · Arthashastra — Chanakya(Kautilya) · Panchatantra — Vishnu Sharma (world's most translated secular work!) · Gitanjali — Tagore (Nobel 1913)\n\n**Holy books:** Hinduism → Vedas, Gita, Upanishads, Ramayana, Mahabharata · Islam → Quran 🕌 · Christianity → Bible ⛪ · Sikhism → Guru Granth Sahib 🙏 · Buddhism → Tripitaka · Jainism → Agamas\n\n**Modern India:** Wings of Fire — APJ Abdul Kalam 🔥 · Discovery of India — Nehru · My Experiments with Truth — Gandhi · Malgudi Days — R.K. Narayan · Train to Pakistan — Khushwant Singh · The God of Small Things — Arundhati Roy (Booker Prize!) · Immortals of Meluha — Amish Tripathi\n\n**World bestsellers:** Bible (~5 billion copies), Quran, Quotations of Mao, Harry Potter series (600M+), LOTR, The Alchemist (Paulo Coelho)\n\n**Kids' classics:** Enid Blyton, Roald Dahl (Charlie & the Chocolate Factory 🍫), Ruskin Bond\n\nA room without books = a body without a soul. Which one are you opening next? 😉"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "gk_firsts", patterns: ["first satellite aryabhata launched","first in india","first prime minister president of india","first indian in space","first woman president of india","chandrayaan missions","first satellite of india","firsts of india gk","rakesh sharma kalpana chawla","first indian to win nobel","bharat ka pehla"],
        responses: ["🥇 **India's hall of FIRSTS:**\n- **First PM:** Jawaharlal Nehru · **First President:** Dr. Rajendra Prasad · **First woman PM:** Indira Gandhi · **First woman President:** Pratibha Patil\n- **First Deputy PM:** Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel (also the Iron Man who united 562 states! 🗿)\n- **First satellite:** **Aryabhata** (1975, named after the mathematician-astronomer) 🛰️\n- **First Indian in space:** Rakesh Sharma (1984) — asked how India looks from space, he said: **'Saare Jahan Se Achcha!'** 🇮🇳\n- **First woman in space (Indian-origin):** Kalpana Chawla (1997, Columbia; honoured forever after the 2003 tragedy) · First Indian woman pilot in IAF combat... keep going, the list is LONG\n- **First Nobel:** Rabindranath Tagore (1913) · First Indian citizen Nobel in science: CV Raman (1930)\n- **First Olympic individual gold:** Abhinav Bindra (2008, shooting) · First track gold: **Neeraj Chopra** (2021, javelin 🥇)\n- **First test-tube baby of India:** Durga (1978, Kolkata)\n- **Moon:** Chandrayaan-1 (2008) discovered water molecules on the Moon! · **Chandrayaan-3 (2023)** = first EVER landing near the lunar south pole 🌙 · Mangalyaan (2014) reached Mars in the FIRST attempt — at less cost than the movie Gravity! 😄🚀"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "gk_festivals", patterns: ["when is diwali celebrated","why is diwali celebrated","festivals of india","diwali holi eid christmas","why do we celebrate diwali","harvest festivals of india","pongal baisakhi onam","durga puja navratri","festival tyohar","raksha bandhan","eid mubarak festival","pushkar camel fair"],
        responses: ["🎉 **India's festival calendar — a party in every season:**\n- **Diwali** 🪔 — the festival of lights (Oct-Nov): Rama's return to Ayodhya after 14 years + defeat of Ravana; Lakshmi puja, sweets, rangoli, crackers (eco ones please! 🌱). Jains celebrate Mahavira's nirvana, Sikhs Bandi Chhor Divas — same lamps, layered stories\n- **Holi** 🎨 — spring's colour splash: victory of devotion (Prahlad & Holika), and Krishna-Radha's playful colours\n- **Eid-ul-Fitr** 🌙 — after Ramadan's month of fasting; Eid-ul-Adha (Bakrid) — sacrifice & sharing\n- **Christmas** 🎄 — 25 Dec, Jesus's birth; cakes, carols, midnight mass\n- **Durga Puja / Navratri** — 9 nights of the Goddess; Garba in Gujarat (world's biggest open-air dance!), pandal-hopping in Bengal\n- **Ganesh Chaturthi** 🐘, **Raksha Bandhan** (sister ties rakhi, brother vows protection 🧵), **Karwa Chauth**, **Makar Sankranti/Pongal/Lohri/Baisakhi** — the great HARVEST festivals (kite flying on Sankranti! 🪁), **Onam** (Kerala's boat races & pookalam flowers 🛶), **Buddha Purnima**, **Mahavir Jayanti**, **Guru Nanak Jayanti**, **Bihu**, **Chhath Puja** (Bihar's soul festival — worshipping the Sun God at riverbanks! 🌅)\n- Also famous: Pushkar camel fair, Rann Utsav, Hornbill festival\n\nIndia = the only country where the calendar needs a committee 😄. Every month is festive!"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "gk_dance", patterns: ["classical dances of india","bharatnatyam kathak","folk dances of india","indian musical instruments","garba bhangra","carnatic hindustani music","dance forms of states","bharat ke nritya","tabla sitar veena","bihar ka lok nritya"],
        responses: ["💃 **Indian dance & music — culture in motion:**\n\n**8 classical dances:**\n- **Bharatanatyam** (Tamil Nadu) — the ancient temple dance, precise geometry\n- **Kathak** (UP/North) — 'storytellers': spins, footwork, tabla battles (Birju Maharaj!)\n- **Kathakali** (Kerala) — 3-hour epics with COLOURFUL face-paint & giant costumes 🎭\n- **Odissi** (Odisha) — fluid tribhanga curves, temple sculptures come alive\n- **Kuchipudi** (Andhra), **Manipuri** (Manipur), **Mohiniyattam** (Kerala), **Sattriya** (Assam)\n\n**Folk/fun:** Bhangra & Giddha (Punjab — harvest energy! 🌾), Garba-Dandiya (Gujarat), Ghoomar (Rajasthan), Chhau (Jharkhand/Bengal/Odisha — martial-art dance!), Lavani (Maharashtra), and Bihar's own **Jat-Jatin & Jhijhiya** 🪔\n\n**Music:** two classical streams — **Hindustani** (North: raga, tabla, sitar, sarod — Ravi Shankar took sitar global, taught George Harrison!) & **Carnatic** (South: veena, mridangam, violin)\n**Instruments:** tabla, sitar, veena, flute (bansuri), sarangi, santoor, shehnai (weddings!), dholak\n\nBollywood mixes all of this with modern beats — and 'Naatu Naatu' won an OSCAR for pure Indian energy 🕺🔥"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "gk_records", patterns: ["tallest statue","statue of unity","tallest statue in the world","world records","tallest longest largest in world","world superlatives gk","highest waterfall longest wall","biggest desert deepest ocean","fastest animal","largest living thing","record todne wale","sabse uncha sabse lamba","worlds biggest stadium"],
        responses: ["🌍 **World records — the biggest, tallest, fastest:**\n\n**Places & nature:**\n- Tallest mountain: **Everest** (8,849m) · Longest river: **Nile** (~6,650km) · Largest ocean: **Pacific** · Deepest point: **Mariana Trench** (~11km — Everest would drown in it!)\n- Biggest desert: **Antarctica** (cold!) / hot: **Sahara** · Largest rainforest: **Amazon** · Highest waterfall: **Angel Falls**, Venezuela (979m)\n- Longest wall: **Great Wall of China** (~21,000km) · Tallest statue: **Statue of Unity**, Gujarat (182m — Sardar Patel, ~2× Statue of Liberty!) 🗽\n- Largest stadium (by capacity): Narendra Modi Stadium, Ahmedabad (132,000!) 🏟️\n- Hottest place: Death Valley (56.7°C) · Coldest: Vostok, Antarctica (−89.2°C)\n\n**Living world:**\n- Largest animal ever: **blue whale** (30m, tongue = elephant's weight) · Tallest animal: giraffe 🦒 · Fastest land animal: cheetah (~110 km/h sprints) · Fastest bird: peregrine falcon (390 km/h dive!) · Largest flower: Rafflesia · Oldest tree: Methuselah bristlecone (~4,850 yrs)\n\n**Human:** fastest human: Usain Bolt (44.7 km/h top speed) · most Oscars: Walt Disney (26!) · youngest Nobel: Malala (17) 🎓"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "gk_currency", patterns: ["currency of uk","currency of britain","currency of united kingdom","currencies of the world","indian rupee","us dollar","currency of japan china uk","exchange rate","which country uses euro","pound sterling yen yuan","mudra ke naam","strongest currency in world","currency symbols list"],
        responses: ["💵 **World currencies — money around the globe:**\n\n**Country → Currency (symbol):**\n- India → **Rupee (₹)** · USA → Dollar ($) · UK → Pound Sterling (£) · EU zone → Euro (€)\n- Japan → Yen (¥) · China → Yuan/Renminbi (¥ — same symbol as yen, different money!) · Russia → Ruble (₽)\n- Saudi Arabia → Riyal · UAE → Dirham · Australia/Canada → their own Dollars (A$/C$) · Switzerland → Swiss Franc (CHF) · South Africa → Rand · Brazil → Real · Bangladesh → Taka · Pakistan → Rupee · Nepal → Rupee · Sri Lanka → Rupee (three cousins!)\n\n**Fun facts:**\n- **Strongest currency:** Kuwaiti Dinar (1 KWD ≈ ₹270+!) — oil wealth 💰\n- **Most traded:** US Dollar (global reserve currency) — oil is priced in dollars\n- **Weirdest history:** salt (Roman 'salary' = salt money!), cowrie shells, giant stone discs (Yap Island — 4m coins you can't carry 🪨)\n- **₹ symbol** = designed 2010 by D. Udaya Kumar: Devanagari 'Ra' + Roman 'R' without the vertical bar, with the tricolour-style double lines!\n- **Exchange rate** = the price of one currency in another; it floats with trade & demand 📈\n- Bitcoin exists too — but that's a crypto-chaos story for another day 😄"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "gk_days", patterns: ["important days and dates","independence day republic day dates","teachers day","environment day","yoga day","world days list","15 august 26 january","international days","diwas kab manaya jata hai","national days of india"],
        responses: ["📅 **The important-days calendar:**\n\n**India's big three:**\n- **26 January** — Republic Day (Constitution生效 1950 — sorry, took effect! 🇮🇳 Rajpath parade, flypast)\n- **15 August** — Independence Day (1947; PM hoists the flag at Red Fort)\n- **2 October** — Gandhi Jayanti + International Day of Non-Violence\n\n**Other national days:** 14 Sept — Hindi Diwas · 5 Sept — Teachers' Day (Dr. Radhakrishnan's birthday!) 🍎 · 14 Nov — Children's Day (Chacha Nehru's birthday 🎈) · 21 June — Yoga Day · 15 Sept — Engineers' Day (M. Visvesvaraya) · 29 Aug — Sports Day (Dhyan Chand) · 26 Nov — Constitution Day · 10 Dec — Human Rights Day (also Nobel day)\n\n**World days:** 22 April — Earth Day 🌍 · 5 June — World Environment Day · 21 April — Civil Services Day · 8 March — Women's Day 💪 · 1 May — Labour Day · 23 April — World Book Day 📚 · 7 April — Health Day · 1 Dec — AIDS Awareness Day · 14 March — Pi Day (3.14! 🥧) · 22 May — Biodiversity Day\n\nTeachers', Children's & Yoga Day are Indian gifts to world calendars. Mark them, celebrate them, learn why! ✍️"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "gk_scientists", patterns: ["missile man","missile man of india","famous scientists","newton einstein","cv raman","abdul kalam","marie curie","scientists and discoveries","who discovered gravity","bharat ratna scientists","great scientists of india","scientist ke yogdan","tesla edison"],
        responses: ["🔬 **Scientist hall of fame:**\n\n**World:**\n- **Isaac Newton** 🍎 — gravity, 3 laws of motion, calculus (co-invented), light = spectrum of colours\n- **Albert Einstein** — E=mc², relativity; Nobel 1921 (for photoelectric effect, funnily NOT relativity!)\n- **Marie Curie** — radioactivity; the ONLY person with Nobels in TWO sciences (Physics 1903 + Chemistry 1911) ⚛️\n- **Nikola Tesla** — AC electricity, induction motor, wireless dreams (Tesla the car brand salutes him) · **Edison** — practical bulb, phonograph, 1,093 patents\n- **Darwin** (evolution), **Galileo** (telescope astronomy — 'yet it moves!'), **Stephen Hawking** (black holes)\n\n**India 🇮🇳:**\n- **CV Raman** — Raman effect (light scattering), Nobel 1930 → 28 Feb = National Science Day\n- **APJ Abdul Kalam** — Missile Man, ISRO/DRDO, then the people's President 🚀; Wings of Fire\n- **Satyendra Nath Bose** — quantum stats; the **Higgs BOSON** is nicknamed 'God particle' but Bose's work named bosons! Einstein co-published with him\n- **Vikram Sarabhai** — father of ISRO · **Homi Bhabha** — nuclear program\n- **Jagadish Chandra Bose** — proved plants respond to stimuli + pioneered radio waves (before Marconi!)\n- **Kalpana Chawla** 🌌, **Tessy Thomas** (Agni Putri), **Nambi Narayanan** (cryogenics — 'Rocketry' film!)\n- Modern: Manjul Bhargava (Fields Medal math), Venki Ramakrishnan (Nobel, ribosomes)"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "gk_fullforms", patterns: ["full forms","what does nasa isro who stand for","abbreviations and full forms","full form of ias ips","computer full forms","full forms list gk","un unesco unicef","wifi sim atm full form","pura roop","acronyms meaning"],
        responses: ["🔤 **Full-form rapid fire:**\n\n**Space & science:** NASA = National Aeronautics and Space Administration 🚀 · ISRO = Indian Space Research Organisation · ESA = European Space Agency · CERN = European Organization for Nuclear Research\n\n**World bodies:** UN = United Nations · UNESCO = UN Educational, Scientific & Cultural Organization · UNICEF = UN Children's Fund · WHO = World Health Organization · WTO = World Trade Organization\n\n**India:** IAS = Indian Administrative Service · IPS = Indian Police Service · RBI = Reserve Bank of India · PM = Prime Minister · MP/MLA = Member of Parliament/Legislative Assembly · UPSC = Union Public Service Commission · GST = Goods & Services Tax\n\n**Tech:** WiFi = Wireless Fidelity (officially it's just a brand name! 😄) · SIM = Subscriber Identity Module · ATM = Automated Teller Machine · URL = Uniform Resource Locator · HTTP = HyperText Transfer Protocol · GPS = Global Positioning System · AI = Artificial Intelligence · PDF = Portable Document Format\n\n**Daily:** PNR = Passenger Name Record · OTP = One-Time Password · MRP = Maximum Retail Price · EMI = Equated Monthly Installment · CV = Curriculum Vitae · BRICS = Brazil-Russia-India-China-South Africa\n\nAbbreviations = language's compression algorithm! 📦"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "gk_isro", patterns: ["pslv satellites record","how many satellites did pslv launch at once","104 satellites in one launch","isro missions","chandrayaan 3","mangalyaan","isro rockets","aditya l1","gaganyaan mission","isro chairman","space research india","isro ke mission","launch pad sriharikota","nasa vs isro"],
        responses: ["🚀 **ISRO — India's space superpower (since 1969, HQ Bengaluru):**\n- **Launch base:** Satish Dhawan Space Centre, **Sriharikota**, Andhra Pradesh (an island! 🏝️)\n- **Rockets:** PSLV — the legendary workhorse (record: **104 satellites in ONE launch**, 2017! 🛰️) · LVM3 (Bahubali) — the heavy lifter for Moon missions · SSLV — small & quick\n\n**Mission wall of fame:**\n- **Chandrayaan-1** (2008) — found WATER on the Moon 💧\n- **Mangalyaan/MOM** (2013–14) — reached Mars in the FIRST attempt (only nation to do so!), built for less than the Hollywood movie 'Gravity' (~₹450 Cr) 😄\n- **Chandrayaan-2** (2019) — orbiter still working perfectly; lander crashed but taught everything\n- **Chandrayaan-3** (Aug 2023) — **FIRST-EVER soft landing at the Moon's south pole!** Vikram lander + Pragyan rover; India = 4th nation to soft-land 🌙🇮🇳\n- **Aditya-L1** (2023) — India's first solar observatory, parked at Lagrange point L1, studying the Sun 24×7 ☀️\n- **Gaganyaan** (coming) — Indian astronauts ('vyomanauts') to orbit! Human spaceflight club: only 3 nations so far\n- **NISAR** (with NASA), **SPADEX** docking demo (2025 — India became 4th nation to master space docking! 🤝)\n\nISRO's superpower = jugaad-grade efficiency: world-class missions at world-lowest costs. Chandrayaan-4 → bring Moon samples home! 🔥"] });

