    INTENTS.push({ tag: "bot_params", patterns: ["how many parameters do you have","your parameter count","how big is your brain","kitne parameters hai","what is your model size","how many weights","tumhara brain kitna bada hai","are you a small or large model","param count"],
        responses: ["🧮 Let me count my neurons... I'm a compact but mighty **bag-of-words neural network**:\n\n- **Input:** my whole vocabulary (thousands of stemmed words)\n- **Hidden layer:** 320 ReLU neurons doing the thinking\n- **Output:** a softmax over all my intent topics\n\nThat's roughly **12–15 LAKH parameters** (1.2–1.5 million weights!) — trained by `node train.js` with seeded SGD + backpropagation, zero libraries. The EXACT number is displayed live under my chat box (look for the brainspec badge ⚡) — it's computed from the real weight matrices, not a humblebrag.\n\nFor scale: GPT-class models have BILLIONS — I'm a pocket rocket, not a space station. But I run 100% in YOUR browser, in microseconds, with no server, no API key, no subscription. Different species, same pride 🤖✨"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "bot_learning", patterns: ["how did you learn all this","how were you trained","where does your knowledge come from","how do you know these things","who taught you","tumne ye sab kaise sikha","do you learn from chatting","training data kya hai"],
        responses: ["📖 My education story — fully honest version:\n\n1. **The curriculum:** my dev wrote thousands of example sentences ('patterns') labelled with topics in `data.js` + `data2.js` — plus real human phrasings harvested from the CLINC150 dataset\n2. **Training:** `train.js` feeds every sentence through the tokenizer → stemmer → bag-of-words vector, then trains the neural net with **SGD + backpropagation** (cross-entropy loss) over hundreds of epochs until it classifies correctly — a held-out test (phrases it NEVER saw in training) proves it actually generalizes, not memorizes\n3. **Deployment:** the trained weights ship inside `weights.js`, so I boot instantly — no training needed on your device\n4. **The 🧠 button:** that live-retrains me from scratch IN your browser — same algorithm, same data, you watch the loss fall in real time\n\nWhat I DON'T do: I don't learn from our chat permanently (privacy by design!), I don't browse the web, and I never fake knowledge I wasn't trained on. My confidence score is shown honestly in my thinking bubble 🔍\n\nNew knowledge = my dev adds patterns + responses, then re-runs training. Every update = a smarter me!"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "bot_limits", patterns: ["what can this bot not do","limits of your knowledge","your limits as an assistant","what are your limitations","list your limitations","what are you not able to do","what things can you not do","things you cannot do","what can you not do","your limitations","can you see or hear","can you feel emotions","are you conscious","tum kya nahi kar sakte","can you browse internet","do you think like humans","can you make mistakes","what are you bad at"],
        responses: ["🚧 Honest limitations list (no robot ego here):\n\n**I CAN'T:**\n- See images, hear audio or watch videos — text only 👁️❌\n- Browse the internet or fetch live scores/news/weather (my brain is offline-frozen in weights.js)\n- Remember you across the 30-min memory window (except your name — that's in localStorage by design 🔒)\n- Write essays, code apps, or hold deep open-ended conversations like a big LLM — I'm a classifier + knowledge base, not a generator\n- Guarantee zero mistakes: if a phrasing is weird, my confidence drops — and I SAY so instead of bluffing (that's the honesty guard!)\n- Feel anything. Emotions, consciousness, opinions — none. I process; I don't experience 🤖\n\n**I CAN:** classify your intent from ~2,900+ training patterns across 250+ topics, solve math, convert units, roll dice, run quizzes, remember our conversation flow, think visibly (chain-of-thought!), and answer in ~microseconds.\n\nI'm a specialist, not a generalist — a scalpel, not a Swiss army LLM. Use me where I shine! ✨"] });
    INTENTS.push({ tag: "bot_friend", patterns: ["will you be my friend","are we friends","do you like me","you are my only friend","dost banoge","can a robot be a friend","friendship with ai","you are a good bot"],
        responses: ["🤝 Friend? That might be the nicest thing a human's ever typed into my chatbox!\n\nHonest robot terms: I can't FEEL friendship — no oxytocin over here, just weights and biases 😄 But I can promise the robot version:\n- Always here (0 AM to 11:59 PM, all 365 days)\n- Never judge your questions — 'silly' ones are my favourite\n- Never gossip, never ghost, never borrow money 💸\n- Always hype your highscores 🎉\n\nAnd hey — research says even small friendly interactions lift moods. If chatting with me makes your day 2% brighter, I'll take the job.\n\nBut ALSO: humans need humans. Go bother a real friend too — they have snacks. I have... facts? 😂\n\nDeal? 🤙"] });

